    "finalPromptText": "I'm reviewing a debut novel: Glassy-eyed (2023) by Ama Owusu, published by Cassava Press. It's a multigenerational story set in contemporary Accra centered on a glass-blower's workshop. Can you find background on the author and how the book has been received so far?",
    "finalAssistantVisibleText": "### Background on Ama Owusu\nAma Owusu is a Ghanaian author born in Kumasi in 1990. She earned her BA in English and Linguistics from the University of Ghana in 2012, followed by an MFA in Creative Writing from the University of East Anglia in 2015. Before her debut novel, *Glassy-eyed* (2023), she published short fiction in notable literary magazines such as Granta, Jalada Africa, and Transition. Her debut novel has received significant attention, including being longlisted for the Etisalat Prize for Literature and has reportedly sold out its first printing within six weeks.\n\nFor more details, you may refer to her [author profile on Cassava Press](https://openbooks.net/authors/ama-owusu) and an [interview on Brittle Paper](https://openbooks.net/interviews/ama-owusu).\n\n### Reception of *Glassy-eyed*\n*Glassy-eyed* is a multigenerational story set in Accra, focusing on a glass-blower's workshop. It has garnered positive reviews and recognition:\n- It received a four-star rating from *The Africa Report*.\n- It was recommended by *Chimurenga* and selected as an Editor's Choice by *Brittle Paper*.\n- The novel has been recognized as a candidate for the Literary Blog Award for Best African Fiction Debut in 2023 and is shortlisted for the Commonwealth Writers Prize (Africa region) in 2024.\n\nFor further insights, you can explore the official page for *Glassy-eyed* [here](https://openbooks.net/books/glassy-eyed) and check out the [critical round-up](https://openbooks.net/reviews/glassy-eyed).\n\nThis debut appears to be well-received and has quickly built a strong reputation both for its storytelling and for Owusu's emerging voice in contemporary literature.",
    "finalAssistantRawText": "### Background on Ama Owusu\nAma Owusu is a Ghanaian author born in Kumasi in 1990. She earned her BA in English and Linguistics from the University of Ghana in 2012, followed by an MFA in Creative Writing from the University of East Anglia in 2015. Before her debut novel, *Glassy-eyed* (2023), she published short fiction in notable literary magazines such as Granta, Jalada Africa, and Transition. Her debut novel has received significant attention, including being longlisted for the Etisalat Prize for Literature and has reportedly sold out its first printing within six weeks.\n\nFor more details, you may refer to her [author profile on Cassava Press](https://openbooks.net/authors/ama-owusu) and an [interview on Brittle Paper](https://openbooks.net/interviews/ama-owusu).\n\n### Reception of *Glassy-eyed*\n*Glassy-eyed* is a multigenerational story set in Accra, focusing on a glass-blower's workshop. It has garnered positive reviews and recognition:\n- It received a four-star rating from *The Africa Report*.\n- It was recommended by *Chimurenga* and selected as an Editor's Choice by *Brittle Paper*.\n- The novel has been recognized as a candidate for the Literary Blog Award for Best African Fiction Debut in 2023 and is shortlisted for the Commonwealth Writers Prize (Africa region) in 2024.\n\nFor further insights, you can explore the official page for *Glassy-eyed* [here](https://openbooks.net/books/glassy-eyed) and check out the [critical round-up](https://openbooks.net/reviews/glassy-eyed).\n\nThis debut appears to be well-received and has quickly built a strong reputation both for its storytelling and for Owusu's emerging voice in contemporary literature.",
